# Delvers S1E05 — Maximum Montage

**Source-identity follow-up, 2026-10-27:** The [S1E07–S1E03 batch check](../../reports/DELVERS_S1E07_S1E03_SOURCE_IDENTITY_2026-10-27.md#s1e05) verifies all comparison inputs listed in the historical report against their recorded Git blobs after CRLF-to-LF conversion only, and verifies their exact historical source paths in the recorded source commit. Raw bytes differ in line endings. This independently confirms local content correspondence with the originally pinned source revision. Earlier provenance statements remain dated history. Prior interpretive coverage, inter-ASR measurements, played cutoff and audio status are unchanged.

**Status:** Played Delvers season-one session, ASR-provisional research (2026-10-24). **Original publication:** spreadsheet lists *Maximum Montage* as S1E05, **2021-02-08**; exact recording day not established. Opening host says they are broadcasting before the Super Bowl, not that the story occurs on that date. **Campaign:** Delvers, a separate continuity from Wastes and Inverse.

**Source integrity:** Entire processed Parakeet transcript read chronologically through the network outro (02:34:40.670). Entire Qwen/Q8 export parsed for comparison and selectively cross-read for significant claims (not independently close-read line by line). Neither audio nor local MP3/SRT alignment was checked. [Full ASR report](../../reports/DELVERS_S1E05_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-24.md) gives exact token methodology and confidence limits. The opening interrogation-like interview is **stylized recap**: Koh humorously minimizes the hardships of the grick expedition, not a new detention or in-world deposition.

